@startuml
!include style.iuml
' Sources: Client.cpp; Server.cpp::admit/dispatchJobs; Controller.cpp;
' StepperMotor.cpp; Sequence.hpp; common/icc/catalog/actions.hpp.
title Raw motor command · the StepperMotor worker path
caption Existing motor commands bypass Robot/Planner and the coordinated Executor program path.
footer This diagram describes current source behavior. Action acceptance and successful execution are distinct events.
autonumber
actor "CLI" as CLI
box "M7 · UI" #EDF4FE
participant "Client\nretained job / action" as C
end box
boundary "Serialized ICC" as W #FFF5DF
box "M4 · IO" #EAF7F4
participant "Server\nIO dispatcher" as S
participant "Controller\n+ Ownership" as O
participant "StepperMotor\nselected motor" as M
participant "STEP HAL\nshared TIM2 / DMA" as H
end box

CLI -> C : submit(MotorGoal)\nshaft angle / rpm / dynamics / BufferMode
C -> C : allocate job ID; retain PendingGoal
C -> W : normal io/motor/motion goal
C --> CLI : job ID; prompt returns
W -> S : admit(goal, ActionExecution)
S -> S : validate goal / command generation / readiness
S -> O : reserveMotor(job, motor)
O -> O : reject Axis / Robot ownership conflicts
alt Rejected or capacity exhausted
  O --> S : Busy owner / rejection
  S --> W : rejected action
  W --> C : terminal rejection
else Motor family admitted
  O --> S : ownership granted
  S --> W : action accept()
  W --> C : accepted callback
  S -> O : moveRel() / moveAbs()\ncompletion observer
  O -> M : submit to selected motor
  alt New active move
    M -> M : create motion worker\n16 KiB stack + runtime allocations
  else Allowed buffered / blended successor
    M -> M : apply existing bounded queue rules
  end
  M --> O : future<Result>
  O --> S : future<Result> (local M4 object only)
  note over S,M #FFF5DF
    Raw action acceptance precedes launching the motor worker.
    A later launch failure produces Faulted, not a successful move.
  end note
  M -> M : runCommands() / CommandRunner\nbuild Profile + Sequence
  M -> H : configure / start selected IStepOutput
  loop Until completion, stop or fault
    H -> H : generate hardware STEP edges
    H -->> M : progress / completion notification
    M -> M : update accounting; wait for notification
    S -> W : action feedback + latest motor-state topic
    W --> C : dispatch progress / state
  end
  M -> M : stop active output; complete(current command)
  M -->> S : completion observer sets ready flag + wakes server
  par Motor worker continues
    M -> M : take next buffered command\nor finishQueue() and return
  else Server dispatches the completed job
    S -> S : get ready future; determine result
    S -> W : succeed / cancelled / abort
    S -> O : releaseJob(job)
    W --> C : terminal callback; keep history
  end
  note over S,M #FFF5DF
    Current raw completion reports a command result before the
    worker necessarily returns. Ordinary completion does not join it.
    The sequential robot-homing path explicitly calls stopAndWait().
  end note
end
note over O,H #EAF7F4
  Other raw motors may run independently; same-motor buffering retains ownership.
  Raw motor stop is immediate cessation, not the Executor's coordinated brake.
  A raw stop targeting a robot-owned member aborts its whole group.
end note
@enduml
